{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040578-quick-question-important-npc-sheets","id":1040578,"title":"Quick Question: Important NPC sheets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-30T05:25:00-08:00","id":1040578,"title":"Quick Question: Important NPC sheets","content":"Given that some NPC types get special treatments, applying attributes, abilities, skills, advantages, different types of virtue/vice, merits, and equipment both available to players and standard NPCs - and, more interestingly, some which are not - what are the types of sheets anyone here thinks would make their lives just a little bit easier in terms of bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> I'm very aware that not having a sheet, or sticking to existing sheets, is just fine for some; it can even be preferable to some styles of play. I'm frankly not interested in that viewpoint, though I respect its perspective.<br /> <br /> Seeing an expanded spirit sheet focused on geister before the release of Geist 2e is something I'm interested in. I'll be taking a crack at it in the interim, putting the standard spirit/ghost abilities on as a cheat-sheet alongside [sadly homebrewed] advancement rules, a section for keys and more in-depth anchors, as well as sections for abilities other than Numina.<br /> <br /> I may also be taking a crack at a Hero sheet, though that's likely much simpler with only Anathema really setting them apart (unless I'm very wrong). Also for B:tP, I'm working on more tangible Horror mechanics which I may apply as an ST, which may lead to a guess-block of sorts, though this seems like something I'd rather avoid letting players get their hands on over just using them as a guideline for internal consistency.<br /> <br /> Is there anything else that people are interested in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","user":"Necrophear","date":". 02-02-2017, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:19:34-08:00","id":1041395,"title":"","content":"I adapted one of Mr. Gone's <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B4JvzOuakdDsZGtIdWVRMWROOU0\" target=\"_blank\">SAS character sheets</a> to second edition for this purpose. I also made an <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B4JvzOuakdDsNVU1TTl4azIxOWM\" target=\"_blank\">ephemeral entity</a> version and a <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B4JvzOuakdDsWjF6UlQ2NkRSTzA\" target=\"_blank\">1/4 page stat block</a> version for minor NPCs. You're welcome to use them if you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-31-2017, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T04:21:06-08:00","id":1041760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-ca